From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 05:56:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Add the SD card
 detect GPIO

The SD slot has a card detect switch, but the board file does not
describe it. The MMC core then only looks for a card once at probe, so a
card inserted or swapped later is not seen.

The switch is wired to PF6 and reads high with a card in the slot. The
board has no pull resistor on it, so request it as active high with the
pull-down of the pin.

Not covered: a card detect interrupt.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; sunxi-mmc gets the
card-detect GPIO, which reads high with a card inserted.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index 55e1dabb6c1f..d812f45e1751 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -77,6 +77,7 @@ reg_vcc3v3: vcc3v3 {
 
 &mmc0 {
 	vmmc-supply = <&reg_vcc3v3>;
+	cd-gpios = <&pio 5 6 (GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH | GPIO_PULL_DOWN)>; /* PF6 */
 	bus-width = <4>;
 	no-mmc;
 	no-sdio;
